Board configuration for FreeBSD on the StarFive VisionFive 2, so that a
freshly built system comes up configured rather than needing to be set up by
hand on the board.

Provides the vf2_display service, which loads the display, GPU and video
decoder modules and programs an HDMI mode. The mode is needed for more than
the picture: the HDMI transmitter derives its audio clock regeneration from
the TMDS clock of the mode it is sending, so HDMI audio does not work until
something sets one, and nothing else does on a headless boot.

Also installs loader tunables for the board as a sample file, leaving
/boot/loader.conf to the administrator.
